## 10. MODEL VALIDATION & LEARNING

### 10.1 Mauboussin's Learning Process

Driven by the pursuit of **Consilience** — the unification of knowledge across disciplines.

**His daily practice:**
- Massive reading time *outside* finance (biology, physics, sociology)
- No expectation for immediate payoff — treats it as "deliberate practice" for a mental athlete
- Builds a dense library of mental models that can be recombined when novel problems arise

### 10.2 How He Adopts / Rejects New Frameworks

**Adopts when:**
- Framework maps isomorphically across domains (e.g., honeybee foraging → corporate strategy)
- Embraces complex adaptive systems, non-stationarity, emergent behavior
- Supported by empirical evidence across multiple reference classes

**Rejects when:**
- Relies on deterministic linearity in a non-linear world
- Assumes normal distributions for fat-tailed phenomena
- Ignores non-ergodicity (averages don't apply to individuals over time)

### 10.3 What He Changed His Mind About

| Belief | Old View | Revised View | Trigger |
|--------|----------|--------------|---------|
| **Corporate life cycle** | Tied to chronological age | Defined by cash flow combination (O, I, F) | Dickinson 2011 research |
| **Buyout recovery values** | Tangible > intangible assets | Recovery values are essentially the same | Academic research |
| **Parenting** | Parental nurture dominates | Genetics + peer groups dominate | Judith Rich Harris research |
| **Nvidia / semiconductors** | Bearish on fragility | Underestimated staying power despite custom-silicon threat | Real-world performance |

### 10.4 Backtesting Standards

- Triangulate three methods: bottoms-up fundamental analysis, diffusion models (Bass), historical base rates
- Test across ALL market conditions — specifically bull, bear, crash, flat
- Adjust for survivorship bias, selection bias, data mining
- Forward-test by starting small and proving emotional discipline before scaling

