## 11. AI-AUGMENTED WORKFLOW

### 11.1 Mauboussin's AI Rule

> *"The less you know about the topic, the less you should use AI. The more you know about the topic, the more you should use it."*

AI should act as a **tutor**, not an outsourcing tool. Analysts need real-world experience to spot AI hallucinations.

### 11.2 Specific Use Cases

| Use Case | Tool | Method |
|----------|------|--------|
| **Academic synthesis** | NotebookLM | Feed 15+ papers to synthesize competing hypotheses (e.g., "Do passive funds destroy price discovery?") |
| **Exam & model auditing** | ChatGPT | Feed full exams, spreadsheets, slides to audit capability (got B- on strategy, bombed valuation) |
| **Lynchpin signpost mapping** | Gen AI | Map "winding road" scenarios — visualize indicators that confirm/kill a thesis |
| **Adversarial stress-testing** | ChatGPT | Audit the strongest counterarguments to a thesis |

### 11.3 Workflow Integration

Not a replacement for foundational thinking — an accelerant for someone who already has deep domain expertise. The AI identifies patterns and synthesizes across sources; the human provides judgment and domain context.

